 Reproducible in: v4.4.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable unknown - Arch Linux #1 ZEN SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Tue, 29 Apr 2025 09:23:22 +0000 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Mesa Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (RPL-P) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900H (20 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn the Compatibility renderer, when using lightmaps, objects marked as Dynamic get ambient light from the sky in addition to the light from the lightmap probes, making them look too bright.\n\nForward+:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/001e1a83-8ec7-4161-afea-6685b024f66c)\n\nCompatibility:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/76fb6915-aee3-4f65-9e32-c0348a3099ef)\n\nCompatibility, with the sky contribution set to 0:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a7eb13ed-43a2-4891-a9a5-f66283832061)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a project with the Forward+ renderer\n2. Create a new scene\n3. Add a WorldEnvironment with a panorama sky\n4. Add some meshes, set some of them to static with UV2, and some to dynamic\n5. Add a LightmapGI and then bake it\n6. Switch to the Compatibility renderer\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[lambiance_de_les_lights.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20048123/lambiance_de_les_lights.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_